     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-18 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Chirag Paswan Criticizes Congress and Announces LJP UP Election Plans</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Union Minister Chirag Paswan has dismissed the Congress party's electoral prospects, asserting that it will not return to power in 2029 or 2034. Paswan accused the party of attempting to incite unrest and instability in India for political gain, comparing their actions to political situations in countries like Bangladesh and Nepal.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/chirag-paswan-criticizes-congress-and-announces-ljp-up-elect.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Separately, Paswan announced that his Lok Janshakti Party (Ram Vilas) will contest the upcoming Uttar Pradesh Assembly elections, regardless of potential alliance arrangements. The party plans to organize a Nav Sankalp Sabha in the state in early November and celebrate its foundation day in Lucknow.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the key political statements and the upcoming party plans in a concise manner.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/chirag-paswan-congress-2034-ljp-ram-vilas-uttar-pradesh-assembly-elections-3020163-2026-10-18?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
