     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · The Hindu World · 2026-10-18 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Donald Trump Blames Immigration for Violent Protests in France</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>U.S. President Donald Trump has linked the recent violent protests in France to immigration, urging the country to close its borders. His comments follow widespread unrest that resulted in 1,800 arrests and the torching of a historic town hall, placing significant pressure on President Emmanuel Macron as national elections approach.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/donald-trump-blames-immigration-for-violent-protests-in-fran.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Vice President JD Vance echoed these sentiments, criticizing Western liberal policies regarding diversity and assimilation. While government officials have blamed &quot;ultra-left&quot; groups for the violence, the situation remains tense as protests against high inflation continue across major French cities including Paris, Marseille, and Lyon.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the political statements but attributes the U.S.-Iran war as the cause of French inflation, which the source presents as a claim within the context of the protest coverage rather than an established fact.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/donald-trump-says-france-is-burning-country-shattered-by-immigration/article71600252.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
