       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SCIENCE</span> · BBC Science · 2026-10-18 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Fuel Leak Spills 25,000 Litres of Kerosene into River Taff</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#science</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A significant fuel leak has contaminated nearly 2.5 miles of the River Taff, with authorities reporting that up to 25,000 litres of kerosene entered the water. Natural Resources Wales (NRW) has identified the source of the pollution and is working to prevent further discharge, though the exact origin remains undisclosed.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/fuel-leak-spills-25000-litres-of-kerosene-into-river-taff.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Residents in affected areas like Taff's Well and Nantgarw have been advised to keep doors and windows shut due to strong fumes. Emergency services are using specialist equipment and absorbent materials to contain the spill, which has caused environmental damage to the river ecosystem.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and includes all essential figures and safety advice provided by the source.</p>
