       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-18 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Jammu Mothers Face Devastation After Storm Destroys Homes and Wedding Savings</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Two mothers in Jammu, Mamta Devi and Sunita Kumar, suffered catastrophic losses during recent heavy rains that ruined their daughters' upcoming wedding preparations. A government hospital boundary wall in Bakshi Nagar collapsed onto Mamta's home, destroying her kitchen, belongings, and cash savings while injuring her and her daughter.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/jammu-mothers-face-devastation-after-storm-destroys-homes-an.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In a separate incident 12 kilometers away in Dream City, Sunita Kumar's residence was flooded after a government nullah became choked. Both families, who were saving for weddings scheduled within the next two to three months, now face homelessness and financial ruin without immediate government support or compensation.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively captures the tragedy and the specific circumstances of both families, though it omits the husband's occupation details.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/jammu-wall-collapse-two-mothers-two-daughters-one-shattered-dream-of-a-wedding-ws-klrt-10387256.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/jammu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Jammu</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
