       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-18 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Karnataka Food Safety Wing Penalizes Sweet Units for Violations</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Karnataka Food Safety Wing conducted a two-day inspection of sweet manufacturing units and sales outlets on October 15 and 16 ahead of the festive season. Officials issued notices to 25 establishments for violations including unhygienic storage, lack of medical fitness certificates for handlers, and improper labelling. Two operators in Kolar district were fined a total of ₹7,000 for these infractions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/karnataka-food-safety-wing-penalizes-sweet-units-for-violati.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During the second day of the drive, authorities inspected 90 units and collected 145 food samples for laboratory analysis. Establishments facing scrutiny include various outlets in Bengaluru, Kalaburagi, Raichur, and Mysuru Rural. The inspections aimed to ensure compliance with food safety and standards across the state.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and includes all essential figures and findings from the provided text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/food-safety-violations-found-at-sweet-units-7000-penalty-imposed-during-second-day-inspections/article71592786.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
