       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-18 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kerala Home Minister Promises Thorough Nedumbassery Crash Probe</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Kerala Home Minister Ramesh Chennithala has pledged a transparent, &quot;zero compromise&quot; police investigation into the Nedumbassery car accident that killed three youths. The Minister dismissed allegations of political interference and criticized media reports that linked government leaders to the case, labeling the incident a &quot;murder&quot; that should not be politicized.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/kerala-home-minister-promises-thorough-nedumbassery-crash-pr.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Meanwhile, Alappuzha police have registered a case against a DYFI leader and a television journalist for allegedly defaming Assembly Deputy Speaker Shanimol Osman by connecting her to the investigation. Chennithala stated that investigators will examine all aspects of the case, including the background of 19-year-old prime accused Suhail Sajeev.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reports on the Home Minister's statements and the legal actions taken regarding the defamation allegations.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/nedumbassery-accident-ramesh-chennithala-promises-zero-compromise-in-probe-slams-alleged-defamation-attempts/article71595706.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
