       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-18 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Mother of Kerala Mini Cooper Crash Accused Expresses Support for Victims</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Nooha, the mother of 19-year-old Suhail, the accused driver in a fatal Mini Cooper crash in Nedumbassery, has publicly offered her condolences and support to the victims' families. Three young people died in the October 11 incident, which police allege involved speeding and driving under the influence of alcohol.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/mother-of-kerala-mini-cooper-crash-accused-expresses-support.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Authorities are moving to suspend or cancel Suhail's driving license following a formal recommendation from police. The Motor Vehicles Department has issued a show-cause notice to the accused, who must respond within 14 days. Nooha has called for a fair investigation into the crash while requesting privacy for her family.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, balanced, and contains all relevant details from the source regarding the accident and the legal proceedings.</p>
