     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · Engadget · 2026-10-18 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>OpenAI CEO Sam Altman Prioritizes Robot 'Brain' in Humanoid Development</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#OpenAI</span> <span>#Robotics</span> <span>#AI</span> <span>#Humanoid</span></div>
       <p>OpenAI CEO Sam Altman is pursuing the development of a humanoid robot, envisioning a machine capable of operating effectively within environments designed for human interaction. This ambition highlights the company's focus on advanced robotics.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/openai-ceo-sam-altman-prioritizes-robot-brain-in-humanoid-de.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>According to Altman, the primary hurdle in this endeavor is not the physical construction of the robot's body, but rather the creation of a sophisticated 'brain'. He identifies the cognitive aspect as a significantly larger challenge in achieving a truly capable humanoid.</p><p>What to watch: Progress on AI 'brains' for humanoid robots.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is a concise and accurate summary of the provided source material regarding OpenAI's humanoid development goals.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.engadget.com/2285040/openai-humanoid-robot-sam-altman-statement-real-challenge/" rel="noopener">Engadget</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
