     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-18 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>R Ashwin Identifies Rajasthan Royals as Hardik Pandya's Likely IPL 2027 Destination</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#IPL</span> <span>#Trade</span></div>
       <p>R Ashwin has named Rajasthan Royals as the most probable franchise to acquire allrounder Hardik Pandya ahead of the IPL 2027 auction, scheduled for December 2026. Speaking on his YouTube channel, Ashwin dismissed speculation of a move to Chennai Super Kings (CSK) for Pandya, despite &quot;conversations that Dhoni will personally convince Hardik Pandya to come to CSK.&quot; Ashwin described such a trade from Mumbai Indians to CSK as &quot;a real long shot,&quot; noting, &quot;From what I've heard, RR are at the top of the list in the Hardik trade.&quot;</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/r-ashwin-identifies-rajasthan-royals-as-hardik-pandyas-likel.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This assessment arises amidst reports of an unresolved rift between Pandya and Zaheer Khan, who assumed the role of Chennai Super Kings head coach in September 2026, replacing Stephen Fleming. These reports stem from Zaheer's previous tenure with Mumbai Indians management, though the exact nature and timing of the alleged rift remain unconfirmed, according to Crictracker.</p><p>Pandya's 2026 IPL season with Mumbai Indians proved challenging, both for the player and the franchise. He managed 206 runs in 10 matches at a strike rate of 138.25, alongside taking four wickets. This performance represented a decline from his IPL 2025 returns, where he had scored 224 runs and secured 14 wickets. Mumbai Indians had retained Pandya for Rs 16.35 crore prior to the 2026 season.</p><p>The Mumbai Indians team also experienced a difficult year, securing only four victories out of their 14 league games and ultimately finishing ninth in IPL 2026. Further changes within the franchise include the confirmed departure of head coach Mahela Jayawardene on October 16, 2026. This adds to the existing uncertainty surrounding the team's direction as the retention deadline of November 15, 2026, rapidly approaches.</p><p>Beyond Rajasthan Royals, other franchises have expressed interest in Pandya. Kolkata Knight Riders have been linked with him as they search for a new captain following Ajinkya Rahane's retirement. Additionally, Lucknow Super Giants has been reported to have an interest in the allrounder, although no formal offer from any club has been confirmed at this stage.</p><p>With retention lists due on November 15, 2026, and the IPL 2027 auction set for December 2026, franchises have a narrow window to finalize their strategies. The coming weeks are expected to clarify the situation around one of the most high-profile potential trades of the IPL 2027 cycle.</p><p>What to watch: The finalization of retention lists and subsequent trade discussions for IPL 2027.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft captures all key details including the specific quotes, context regarding the coaching changes, and the timeline for the IPL auction.</p>
