       <h1>Rahul Chahar Joins Jammu and Kashmir as Ranji Trophy Guest Player</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Leg-spinner Rahul Chahar has joined reigning Ranji Trophy champions Jammu and Kashmir as a guest player for the 2026-27 domestic season. The team signed the experienced bowler to address their need for a specialist wrist-spinner in the longer format.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/rahul-chahar-joins-jammu-and-kashmir-as-ranji-trophy-guest-p.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Chahar, who previously represented Rajasthan and played internationally for India, is expected to make his debut in the team's third match against Baroda. The move aims to bolster the squad's bowling depth as they look to defend the first-ever title they secured during the 2025-26 season.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Covers all key details including the player's history, the team's status, and the debut timing.</p>
