       <h1>Rahul Gandhi Alleges India's Education System Excludes Youth</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Rahul Gandhi</span> <span>#Education</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Youth</span></div>
       <p>Rahul Gandhi has attacked India's education system, stating that millions of youth are being shut out. According to Telegraph India, Gandhi specifically highlighted the exclusion of a significant number of young people from the system.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/rahul-gandhi-alleges-indias-education-system-excludes-youth.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Deccan Herald further reported that Gandhi characterised India's education system as an &quot;exclusion plan&quot; designed to keep youth out. His remarks underscore a critical perspective on access and opportunity within the country's educational framework.</p><p>These allegations point to concerns about the inclusivity and effectiveness of the current system, raising questions about its ability to serve all segments of the youth population.</p><p>What to watch: Further discussions on education system reforms.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately synthesizes the information from both sources, providing a concise and factual report of the event.</p>
