       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-10-18 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Sugarcane: Beyond Sweetness, A Plant of Many Uses for India's Economy</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Sugarcane</span> <span>#Agriculture</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Sustainability</span></div>
       <p>Sugarcane, a common feature of India's agricultural landscape, offers far more than just its sweet juice and traditional sweeteners like sugar and jaggery. A significant crop, India produced 454.61 million tonnes in 2024-25, according to the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare’s Agricultural Statistics at a Glance. This volume highlights its potential for diverse applications beyond food.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/sugarcane-beyond-sweetness-a-plant-of-many-uses-for-indias-e.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Research by Indian agricultural institutions, as explored in &quot;1 Plant, 100 Uses,&quot; reveals sugarcane's extensive utility. Its fibrous residue, known as bagasse, can be used for generating electricity in sugar mills, with surplus power potentially supplied to the grid, noted by the Ministry of New and Renewable Energy. Bagasse also serves as a raw material for paper production and can be processed into compostable tableware, a technology developed by ICAR’s Central Institute for Research on Cotton Technology, capable of producing 10,000 to 30,000 plates daily.</p><p>Furthermore, other by-products contribute significantly. Press mud, or filter cake, can enrich agricultural soil as compost, returning organic matter to farmland. The green tops and leaves left after harvest provide valuable dry fodder for cattle, particularly when conventional feed is scarce, as per an ICAR study. The Institute of Wood Science and Technology also highlights bagasse's use in manufacturing particle boards for furniture and interior applications.</p><p>Why it matters: Maximizing sugarcane's diverse uses can reduce waste and create economic value for farmers and industries.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes the provided source, covering statistics, industrial applications, and the various uses of sugarcane as described.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/sustainability/how-every-part-of-sugarcane-plant-used-in-india-12671817" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
