       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-10-18 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Trump Mocks French Unrest as Protests Escalate</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>US President Donald Trump mocked the violent protests sweeping France, sarcastically labeling the country an ideal destination for revolutions as demonstrations over living costs turned into widespread looting and arson. The unrest, which saw hundreds of thousands participate, resulted in clashes with police, destruction of luxury retail outlets, and fires across multiple cities.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/trump-mocks-french-unrest-as-protests-escalate.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Vice President JD Vance attributed the violence to failed Western liberal immigration policies, arguing that a lack of cultural assimilation triggered the chaos. Vance warned that the situation in France reflects the future congressional Democrats intend for the United States, urging French authorities to restore order before further landmarks are damaged.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Captures Trump's and JD Vance's remarks and the context of the French protests accurately based on the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/lets-go-to-france-lovely-place-trump-mocks-violent-protests-looting-and-fires-ws-l-10387201.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
