    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/finance">finance</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-10-18 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>UIDAI Issues Comprehensive Document List for Aadhaar Updates</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Unique Identification Authority of India (UIDAI) has released a list of accepted documents for individuals seeking to update their name, address, date of birth, or relationship details in their Aadhaar. Required documentation varies based on the specific information being modified, with some records serving multiple purposes and others restricted to single categories.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/uidai-issues-comprehensive-document-list-for-aadhaar-updates.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Applicants must provide valid proof of identity, address, or date of birth as specified by UIDAI guidelines. Documents such as passports, ration cards, voter IDs, and government-issued certificates are generally accepted to verify personal details. Holders are advised to ensure their chosen documentation meets the authority’s specific verification standards for processing updates.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the document guidelines released by UIDAI for Aadhaar updates without any hallucination.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
