     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-18 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>YSRCP Withdraws From Punganur Civic Polls Amid Security Concerns</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The YSR Congress Party (YSRCP) has opted to skip the Punganur municipality elections, citing a lack of transparency and security threats to its candidates. MLA Peddireddi Ramachandra Reddy announced the decision following violent clashes between YSRCP and TDP supporters on the first day of nominations, which resulted in multiple cases being filed against party workers.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-18/ysrcp-withdraws-from-punganur-civic-polls-amid-security-conc.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Local authorities have subsequently issued notices to MLA Peddireddi Ramachandra Reddy and MP P.V. Midhun Reddy, prohibiting them from entering Punganur town to maintain law and order. Police have increased security in the area to prevent further confrontation during the ongoing nomination process.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively captures the core conflict, the YSRCP's withdrawal, and the official police response.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/andhra-pradesh-ysrcp-to-skip-punganur-civic-body-polls-peddireddi-midhun-reddy-told-to-stay-away-from-town/article71599669.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
